From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] interconnect: qcom: Add MSM8998 interconnect provider
 driver

Add an icc-rpm based interconnect provider driver for MSM8998,
modelled on the MSM8996 driver (the neighbouring SoC generation) with
the topology transcribed from the downstream msm8998-bus.dtsi:
A1NOC, A2NOC, BIMC, CNOC, GNOC (virtual; hosts the apps-proc master),
MNOC and SNOC, 107 nodes in total.  The downstream MMSS-AHB config
fabric is folded into the MNOC provider, following what the MSM8996
driver does with the mmagic config slaves; its bus clock is HLOS-owned
and not part of the RPM vote path.

The immediate motivation is RPM sleep-set hygiene: clk-smd-rpm posts
INT_MAX handoff votes for the six RPM bus clocks of this SoC
(bimc/snoc/cnoc/aggre1/aggre2/mmssnoc-axi) in both the active AND the
sleep set at probe, expecting an interconnect driver to take over and
scale them.  MSM8998 never had one, so those votes stay pinned at
INT_MAX forever, which (among other things) forbids the RPM from ever
reaching its low-power states.  With this driver the framework's
sync_state takes the votes down to the aggregated consumer requests.

QoS register programming is intentionally left out of this first
version: no regmap is attached and no qos_mode is set, so probing only
masters the RPM bandwidth and bus-clock votes.  The boot-time QoS
configuration inherited from the bootloader is left untouched, exactly
as before this patch.  keep_alive is set on all clocked providers so
that config-space access keeps a 19.2 MHz floor even before any
consumer votes, matching qcm2290/sm6115.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Kconfig b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Kconfig
@@ -89,6 +89,15 @@
 	  This is a driver for the Qualcomm Network-on-Chip on msm8996-based
 	  platforms.
 
+config INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8998
+	tristate "Qualcomm MSM8998 interconnect driver"
+	depends on INTERCONNECT_QCOM
+	depends on QCOM_SMD_RPM
+	select INTERCONNECT_QCOM_SMD_RPM
+	help
+	  This is a driver for the Qualcomm Network-on-Chip on msm8998-based
+	  platforms.
+
 config INTERCONNECT_QCOM_OSM_L3
 	tristate "Qualcomm OSM L3 interconnect driver"
 	depends on INTERCONNECT_QCOM || COMPILE_TEST
diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Makefile b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Makefile
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/Makefile
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 qnoc-msm8974-objs			:= msm8974.o
 qnoc-msm8976-objs			:= msm8976.o
 qnoc-msm8996-objs			:= msm8996.o
+qnoc-msm8998-objs			:= msm8998.o
 icc-osm-l3-objs				:= osm-l3.o
 qnoc-qcm2290-objs			:= qcm2290.o
 qnoc-qcs404-objs			:= qcs404.o
@@ -57,6 +58,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8974) += qnoc-msm8974.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8976) += qnoc-msm8976.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8996) += qnoc-msm8996.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8998) += qnoc-msm8998.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_OSM_L3) += icc-osm-l3.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_QCM2290) += qnoc-qcm2290.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_QCS404) += qnoc-qcs404.o
